<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.2.5"/>
    <code code="10210-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Physical findings of General status Narrative"/>
    <title>General Status</title>
    <text><paragraph>Alert and engaged. At the first visit, in the on state about two hours after a levodopa dose: Hoehn and Yahr stage 2.5; MDS-UPDRS Part III 30. Bilateral bradykinesia and rigidity, worse on the right; right-hand rest tremor; reduced facial expression and blinking; soft, monotone speech; reduced arm swing with short steps; recovers unaided on the pull test after three steps. No dyskinesia, wearing-off, or freezing. Falls: none in the past year and no near falls; Timed Up and Go 13 seconds without an aid. Orthostatic check at the first visit: 130/80 mmHg, pulse 70, after 5 minutes supine; 122/78 mmHg, pulse 76, after 3 minutes standing, without symptoms; no orthostatic hypotension. Non-motor screens at the first visit: EAT-10 swallowing screen 2 (below the threshold of 3), no choking or coughing with meals; no dream enactment on the RBD screening questionnaire; Epworth Sleepiness Scale 6; no constipation, urinary urgency, or lightheadedness; no hallucinations; impulse-control screen (QUIP-RS) negative. Independent in all activities of daily living; buttoning and handwriting are slow; drives only short local trips in daylight. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

