    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Review the levodopa dose and timing at every visit for slowness, wearing-off, and dyskinesia; take doses 30 minutes before meals; check supine and three-minute standing blood pressure after any change; avoid dopamine-blocking drugs such as metoclopramide, prochlorperazine, and most antipsychotics. Guideline: Dopaminergic Therapy for Motor Symptoms in Early Parkinson Disease Practice Guideline Summary: A Report of the AAN Guideline Subcommittee (2021); The recommendations of a consensus panel for the screening, diagnosis, and treatment of neurogenic orthostatic hypotension and associated supine hypertension (2017); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Parkinson&apos;s disease monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Movement disorders neurology consultation to confirm the diagnosis against the MDS criteria, adjust levodopa, plan rehabilitation, and advise on genetic testing. Guideline: Dopaminergic Therapy for Motor Symptoms in Early Parkinson Disease Practice Guideline Summary: A Report of the AAN Guideline Subcommittee (2021); MDS clinical diagnostic criteria for Parkinson&apos;s disease (2015); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Parkinson&apos;s disease monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Monitor on the CMID schedule: motor examination, Hoehn and Yahr stage, fall check, psychosis and impulse-control questions, and medication review every visit; cognition, mood, sleep, autonomic symptoms, swallowing, speech, and driving yearly; dental examination every six months. Guideline: MDS clinical diagnostic criteria for Parkinson&apos;s disease (2015); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Parkinson&apos;s disease monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Advance care planning: name a health care agent and record goals of care, and revisit with any change in stage. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Parkinson&apos;s disease monograph (2026) [S]</item><item ID="referral-order">Referral to neurology (movement disorders), Kwame Asante, MD, ordered 2026-02-10 [S]</item></list></text>

